Reused (adapted) from packages/core/src/tool/plugin/{edit,read,write}.ts:
  - src/spec/descriptions.rs: the wording of the `edit`, `read` and `write` contracts: omit the
    line-number prefix and keep exact indentation; the match must be unique unless replaceAll;
    add surrounding context to disambiguate; "Writes a file to the local filesystem, overwriting
    if one exists. Missing parent directories are created automatically"; directory listing and
    offset/limit paging of `read`; the 2000-line default and cap.
  - src/edit/{matcher,fold,document}.rs: the design of the tiered edit match (exact, then
    typographic-quote/dash/space normalised, then trailing-whitespace-insensitive), matching
    against an LF view of a CRLF file, and keeping each untouched line's original ending.
    Reimplemented in Rust, not translated line by line.
  - src/edit/hint.rs: the idea of answering a miss with the closest lines, numbered like `read`
    output, and noting when new_string is already in the file.
  - src/patch/ and src/spec/descriptions.rs: the OpenCode `patch` tool description follows
    Codex's (below).

